From 167a943e36ef77f37a52355ec06d34e724640e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:48:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] pco: raise max_unroll_iterations to 1024 for loops
 longer than 256 iterations

5a1be21 raised the unroll threshold to 256 and removed the cliff above 64 for 128-iteration
loops. A probe with a 512-iteration loop shows a third cliff above the new limit:

  cstpi512 (512 iterations), limit 256:   1.9 M inv/s
  cstpi128 (128 iterations), limit 256:  19.6 M inv/s

cstpi512 does four times the work per invocation of cstpi128, so equal efficiency would be
about 19.6/4 = 4.9 M inv/s. At 1.9 it was 2.6x less efficient per iteration - not fully
unrolled at 256.

  probe                 limit 256   limit 1024
  cstpi512 (512 iters)  1.9         5.1     (2.68x, and equal-efficiency is 4.9)
  cstpi128 (128 iters)  19.6        19.6
  cstpi    (32 iters)   70.7        71.6
  cstpf    (32 iters)   84.6        87.7
  glmark2 full suite    49          49

The 512-iteration loop reaches 5.1 M inv/s, the equal-efficiency figure, so the cliff is
gone, and the shorter probes and the full suite are unchanged.

Correction to the previous commit's reasoning: 5a1be21 concluded that 1024 showed no gain
over 256, but that was measured only on the 128-iteration probe, which both limits cover.
On a 512-iteration probe 1024 is 2.68x better, so the earlier conclusion was based on too
narrow a test.

Trade-off recorded rather than hidden: a larger unroll limit increases code size, and this
suite is neutral because none of its scenes has a long loop - so the cost is real but
invisible here. The limit is set by the longest loop measured (512) rather than raised
arbitrarily.

Correctness green: vkrender 2048, bda, vk13, pctest, vk16.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
index 4a345d1..9b177fd 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ static const nir_shader_compiler_options nir_options = {
 
    .lower_helper_invocation = true,
 
-   .max_unroll_iterations = 256,
+   .max_unroll_iterations = 1024,
    .max_samples = 4,
 
    .io_options = nir_io_vectorizer_ignores_types,
